nodes:
- _type: Monitor
  name: SRE · VMware import inventory unavailable · 3m
  identifier: urn:custom:monitor:sre-dashboards:import-inventory
  description: The inventory collector reports unsuccessful or stale reads for 3 minutes
    of observed samples. A completely missing collector produces no series; also check
    the official Agent workload health. No successful import is inferred from absent
    data.
  arguments:
    metric:
      query: max_over_time((max by (cluster_name) (harvester_import_inventory_up))[3m:30s])
      unit: none
      aliasTemplate: ${cluster_name}
    comparator: LT
    threshold: 1
    failureState: DEVIATING
    urnTemplate: urn:cluster:/kubernetes:${cluster_name}
    titleTemplate: SRE · VMware import inventory unavailable · 3m · ${cluster_name}
  intervalSeconds: 60
  status: ENABLED
  remediationHint: Check the obs-imports-imports workload, import-inventory logs,
    VM Import Controller CRD and read permissions. Check metric delivery and the ingestion
    Secret without printing its value. No VMware login or new import is needed to
    repair inventory.
  tags:
  - sre-dashboards
  - dashboard-imports
  function: {{ get "urn:stackpack:common:monitor-function:threshold" }}
